<title>USA: Fed refrains from open market operations.</title>
<headline>Fed refrains from open market operations.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve refrained from open market operations on Friday, as expected, dealers said.</p>
<p>Federal funds were trading at 5-3/8 percent, below the Fed's 5-1/2 percent target for the rate, in morning dealings.</p>
<p>-- ((Ellen Freilich, North American Treasury Desk 212-859-1679))</p>
